Palette mapping
  Base16 and Base24 semantic UI colors follow the systems' role definitions:
    background base00; surface base01; selection background base02;
    border base03; muted foreground base04; foreground/selection foreground
    base05; error base08; warning base0A; success base0B; accent/info base0D.

  Base16 ANSI 0..15 follows the gallery's PREVIEW_ROLE_KEYS mapping:
    00, 08, 0B, 0A, 0D, 0E, 0C, 05,
    03, 08, 0B, 0A, 0D, 0E, 0C, 07.

  Base24 uses the same normal ANSI colors and semantic roles. Its distinct
  bright red/green/yellow/blue/magenta/cyan are base12/base14/base13/base16/
  base17/base15, respectively; bright black and white remain base03/base07.

  Tinted8 ANSI colors use each resolved palette color's normal and bright
  variants in black/red/green/yellow/blue/magenta/cyan/white order. Semantic
  colors use these resolved UI variables from the gallery payload:
    background          ui.global.background.normal
    foreground          ui.global.foreground.normal
    surface             ui.chrome.background.normal
    muted               ui.global.foreground.dark
    border              ui.border.normal
    accent              ui.accent.normal
    selection_bg        ui.selection.background
    selection_fg        ui.selection.foreground
    success             ui.status.success
    warning             ui.status.warning
    error               ui.status.error
    info                 ui.status.info

